---
layout: base.njk
title: Fed Dot Plots in 3D | Benson Fung
description: Every FOMC dot plot since 2012 as an interactive 3D scatter — 59 vintages, 4,627 dots — with the median path and the longer-run neutral rate alongside.
---

<section class="hero-section" style="text-align: left; align-items: flex-start;">
  <p class="hero-tagline" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Fed Dot Plots in 3D</p>
  <h1>Fourteen years of dot plots, in one cloud</h1>
  <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: 680px;">
    Every dot from every FOMC Summary of Economic Projections since January 2012.
  </p>
  <p id="fdp-summary" style="max-width: 680px;">Loading summary…</p>
</section>

<section id="fdp" data-json="{{ '/assets/data/fed-dot-plots.json' | cacheBust }}" aria-label="Fed dot plots 3D chart">
  <details class="fdp-filters">
    <summary>Filters</summary>
    <div class="afm-controls">
    <div class="afm-row">
      <label>SEP vintage from
        <input type="date" id="fdp-vintage-min" value="2012-01-25" min="2012-01-25" max="2026-09-16" aria-label="Earliest SEP vintage">
      </label>
      <label>to
        <input type="date" id="fdp-vintage-max" value="2026-09-16" min="2012-01-25" max="2026-09-16" aria-label="Latest SEP vintage">
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="afm-row">
      <label>Target year from
        <input type="number" id="fdp-year-min" value="2012" min="2012" max="2029" aria-label="Earliest target year">
      </label>
      <label>to
        <input type="number" id="fdp-year-max" value="2029" min="2012" max="2029" aria-label="Latest target year">
      </label>
      <button type="button" class="ft-reset" id="fdp-reset">Reset</button>
      <button type="button" class="ft-reset" id="fdp-reset-view">Reset 3D view</button>
    </div>
    <div class="afm-row">
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="fdp-show-median" checked> Show median path</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="fdp-show-lr" checked> Show Longer run panel</label>
    </div>
    </div>
  </details>
  <p class="afm-legend">
    <span><i style="background: var(--color-accent);"></i>One dot (marker size = number of participants at that rate)</span>
    <span><i style="background: #d97706;"></i>Median path (per vintage × target year)</span>
  </p>

  <p id="fdp-count" role="status">Loading chart…</p>

  <div class="afm-graph">
    <div id="fdp-plot" class="fdp-plot" role="img" aria-label="3D scatter plot of FOMC dot plots: SEP vintage, target year, and federal funds rate"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="fdp-colorbar" aria-hidden="true">
    <span>Colour = SEP vintage</span>
    <div class="fdp-colorbar-bar"></div>
    <div class="fdp-colorbar-ticks">
      <span style="left: 0%; transform: translateX(0);">2012</span>
      <span style="left: 26.8%;">2016</span>
      <span style="left: 54.1%;">2020</span>
      <span style="left: 81.4%;">2024</span>
      <span style="left: 94.9%;">2026</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="afm-detail" id="fdp-detail">
    <p>Hover or tap a dot for detail.</p>
  </div>

  <noscript>
    <p>The chart needs JavaScript. The underlying data is still available as <a href="/assets/data/fed-dot-plots.json">JSON</a>, and the table below is the same data in median form.</p>
  </noscript>

  <div id="fdp-lr-section">
    <h2>Longer run (neutral rate)</h2>
    <div class="afm-graph">
      <div id="fdp-lr-plot" class="fdp-lr-plot" role="img" aria-label="Longer-run dot plots over time: SEP vintage against federal funds rate"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="afm-detail" id="fdp-lr-detail">
      <p>Hover or tap a dot for detail.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Latest SEP — September 16, 2026: medians</h2>
  <div class="afm-table-wrap">
    <table class="afm-table" id="fdp-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Target year</th><th style="text-align: right;">Participants</th><th style="text-align: right;">Median (derived)</th><th style="text-align: right;">Median (published, Table 1)</th><th style="text-align: right;">Range (derived)</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td colspan="5">Loading table…</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <ul class="fdp-sources">
